{"author":{"id":"3f8bad4585cb0f07c6570d9e31f06264af3b0abf48efbc5a44f56df5e7a9cd45"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1789327520,"nonce":"HO3kD/MlSiF0ly0hJW9zWmesQEA=","message":"After the lookup work (release, ash hybrid, wren_lift tiered, 200000\niterations, median of 5, ns per call). wren_lift's baselines moved too:\nits top tier now lands in the same range as Ash's.\n\n                Haxe→Haxe  Wren→Wren  Haxe→Wren  Wren→Haxe\n    static call       3.6        5.2       56.1       71.2\n    method call       3.5        5.6       54.7       84.9\n    getter            3.4        3.6       30.7       51.8\n    setter            0.7        3.8       54.9       50.0\n    closure call      3.5        3.6       81.4       78.3\n    construct         6.2       55.4      355.5      341.9\n\nConstruct varies 300–400 between runs; the full table run also drifts\nunder the cells before it, so a cell alone (`--only`, `--column`) is the\nnumber to compare.\n\nWhat landed, and what each bought (the middle columns, before → after):\n\n- Compiled Wren bodies: `call_closure_jit_or_sync`, then wren_lift's own\n  `dispatch_method_pub` for everything found, with its trivial\n  getter/setter fast path. Static 157→113→67, getter 115→82→42.\n- Signature symbols cached per VM by core symbol and shape, then per\n  call site: no string is hashed on a hit.\n- Direct typed calls into compiled Haxe by signature kinds\n  (`ash_native_call`), `Callable::Cell` reading `functions_ptrs`,\n  fields read and written in place by offset, methods by their table\n  slot: Wren→Haxe static 108→100, getter 103→81, setter 98→74.\n- `CallSite` in the protocol and on every foreign slot/target; the\n  Haxe side's static resolution behind an atomic instead of a mutex;\n  lock-free symbol reads; the typed dispatcher table by language id;\n  an address hasher on the maps consulted per call; stack buffers for\n  arguments on both sides; null handles skip the GC lock.\n- Natives typed by result (`Float`, `Bool`, else `Dynamic`): the Haxe\n  library emits them and caribou-ash binds an entry per result\n  register. Haxe→Wren static 66→56, getter 41→31.\n\nTier awareness: Ash counts a bridge callee through `hlp_dyn_call` while\nit is a stub, so it reaches Cranelift; the direct call then bypasses the\ncounter, which is Ash's own rule (a compiled caller stops ticking its\ncallee) so the LLVM rung is not reached by counting from the bridge\neither. wren_lift's embedder entries did not tick; the protocol now\nticks `record_call` for a constructor and a `Fn`, and `dispatch_method`\nticks a method itself.\n\nWhere the rest is, from `sample` on one cell:\n\nWren→Haxe static (~70): the HashLink trap per call is about a fifth\n(`hlp_setup_trap_jit`/`hlp_remove_trap_jit` go through a RefCell\nthread-local twice, plus `_setjmp`), all Ash's; wren_lift's own native\ndispatch (`wren_call_1_inner`, `dispatch_call`, three `_tlv_get_addr`)\nabout a sixth; the VM thread-local, two address-map lookups (binding by\nclass, instance by address), `catch_unwind` and `settle` the rest.\n\nHaxe→Wren static (~56): Ash boxes each numeric argument\n(`hlp_make_dyn`, an allocation) because the natives' parameters are\n`Dynamic`; wren_lift's `dispatch_method` (two thread-locals,\n`modvars_cell_addr`) about a fifth; the VM thread-local; `catch_unwind`\nand `settle`.\n\nClosure call Haxe→Wren (81) is the var-args path: a `varray` per call\nwith boxed arguments, because a `Fn` parameter is `Dynamic` in Haxe.\n\nCandidates left: arguments unboxed on the Haxe→Wren side, which needs\nthe native called by kinds rather than as pointers — one entry per\nsignature shape is combinatorial, so this wants a convention at Ash's\nlevel (a host native taking its arguments as a record by kind, the way\n`ash_native_call` places them going the other way); a typed `Fn`\nsignature in `#export` so a callback is a typed closure instead of\nvar-args; the trap's cost, which is Ash's try/catch cost; construct,\nwhich allocates the instance, its face or handle, and a map entry on\nboth sides.","files":null}]}